      "widgets_values": [
        "{\"version\":1,\"content\":\"<h1>HOW TO USE</h1><p>\\n\\n</p><p>Makes ONE long picture from a folder of photos, side by side, like a photo booth strip or a before and after row. No AI is used: it shows how a loop can build one result from many pictures.</p><p>\\n\\n</p><hr class=\\\"pix-note-hr-solid\\\" style=\\\"color: #b8b8b8\\\"><p>\\n\\n</p><h2><span data-ic=\\\"folder-v1\\\" class=\\\"pix-note-ic\\\" contenteditable=\\\"false\\\" style=\\\"color: #f66744\\\"></span>&nbsp;Pick your folder</h2><p>\\n\\n</p><ol><li>On <b>Load Images from Folder Pixaroma</b>, click <b>Browse</b> and pick your folder, or paste the folder's path into the box.</li><li>Click <b>Pick images</b>, then <b>Select all</b>, or click only the pictures you want. The button shows how many are picked.</li><li>Press <b>Run</b> once. Leave the Run count at <b>1</b>: the node sends every picture through by itself, one after the other.</li></ol><p>\\n\\n</p><p>This workflow opens with <b>no folder picked</b>: choose your own folder, or try it first on the demo folder <b>Portraits</b> inside the <b>Media Inputs</b> folder that comes with these workflows.</p><p>\\n\\n</p><p><span data-ic=\\\"idea\\\" class=\\\"pix-note-ic\\\" contenteditable=\\\"false\\\" style=\\\"color: #f66744\\\"></span>&nbsp;A folder inside ComfyUI's own <code>input</code> or <code>output</code> folder works straight away. A folder anywhere else works too, but pick it once with <b>Browse</b>: that is how ComfyUI knows you allowed it.</p><p>\\n\\n</p><p><span data-ic=\\\"idea\\\" class=\\\"pix-note-ic\\\" contenteditable=\\\"false\\\" style=\\\"color: #f66744\\\"></span>&nbsp;Pictures go through in name order. Name them <code>01_</code>, <code>02_</code> and so on if the order matters.</p><p>\\n\\n</p><hr class=\\\"pix-note-hr-solid\\\" style=\\\"color: #b8b8b8\\\"><p>\\n\\n</p><h2><span data-ic=\\\"gear\\\" class=\\\"pix-note-ic\\\" contenteditable=\\\"false\\\" style=\\\"color: #f66744\\\"></span>&nbsp;Change the look</h2><p>\\n\\n</p><ul><li>The size of each photo: <b>Resize Crop Pixaroma</b>.</li><li>The gap and its color: <b>spacing_width</b> and <b>spacing_color</b> on <b>Stitch Images</b>.</li><li>A tall strip instead of a wide one: set the direction on Stitch Images to <b>up</b>.</li></ul><p>\\n\\n</p><hr class=\\\"pix-note-hr-solid\\\" style=\\\"color: #b8b8b8\\\"><p>\\n\\n</p><h2><span data-ic=\\\"workflow-v3\\\" class=\\\"pix-note-ic\\\" contenteditable=\\\"false\\\" style=\\\"color: #f66744\\\"></span>&nbsp;How a loop works</h2><p>\\n\\n</p><ul><li>Everything between <b>Loop Start</b> and <b>Loop End</b> runs again and again: <b>total</b> on Loop Start says how many rounds.</li><li>Loop Start's <b>index</b> says which round it is, counting from <b>0</b> (0, 1, 2, 3). A Math Expression turns it into what you need: <code>a + 1</code> for 1, 2, 3, 4, or <code>a + b</code> to add it to a seed.</li><li>The <b>value</b> slots carry things from one round to the next. What you plug into Loop End's value1 comes out of Loop Start's value1 in the NEXT round. After the last round it comes out of Loop End.</li><li>Wire Loop Start's <b>loop</b> output into Loop End's <b>loop</b> input: that is how the two know they belong together.</li></ul><p>\\n\\n</p><p><span data-ic=\\\"idea\\\" class=\\\"pix-note-ic\\\" contenteditable=\\\"false\\\" style=\\\"color: #f66744\\\"></span>&nbsp;This loop needs no count from you: Get Image Size counts the photos and sets the rounds. Wiring a number into total like this works on any loop.</p><p>\\n\\n</p><hr class=\\\"pix-note-hr-solid\\\" style=\\\"color: #b8b8b8\\\"><p>\\n\\n</p><h2><span data-ic=\\\"question-mark\\\" class=\\\"pix-note-ic\\\" contenteditable=\\\"false\\\" style=\\\"color: #f66744\\\"></span>&nbsp;Something not working?</h2><p>\\n\\n</p><p>Each button opens the answer on the Pixaroma help page.</p><p>\\n\\n</p><p><span class=\\\"pix-note-btnblock\\\"><a class=\\\"pix-note-rm\\\" style=\\\"background-color: #f66744\\\" href=\\\"https://workflows.pixaroma.com/help/faq/#q-folder-not-approved\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\" rel=\\\"noopener noreferrer\\\">Folder not approved</a></span>&nbsp;<span class=\\\"pix-note-btnblock\\\"><a class=\\\"pix-note-rm\\\" style=\\\"background-color: #f66744\\\" href=\\\"https://workflows.pixaroma.com/help/faq/#q-save-other-folder\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\" rel=\\\"noopener noreferrer\\\">Save to your own folder</a></span>&nbsp;<span class=\\\"pix-note-btnblock\\\"><a class=\\\"pix-note-rm\\\" style=\\\"background-color: #f66744\\\" href=\\\"https://workflows.pixaroma.com/help/look/\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\" rel=\\\"noopener noreferrer\\\">Nodes look different from the video</a></span>&nbsp;</p><p>\\n\\n</p>\",\"buttonColor\":\"#f66744\",\"lineColor\":\"#f66744\",\"backgroundColor\":\"#2a2a2a\",\"info\":{\"title\":\"How to Use\",\"icon\":\"to-do\",\"color\":\"#2a9d8f\"}}"
      ],
      "widgets_values_named": {
        "note_json": "{\"version\":1,\"content\":\"<h1>HOW TO USE</h1><p>\\n\\n</p><p>Makes ONE long picture from a folder of photos, side by side, like a photo booth strip or a before and after row. No AI is used: it shows how a loop can build one result from many pictures.</p><p>\\n\\n</p><hr class=\\\"pix-note-hr-solid\\\" style=\\\"color: #b8b8b8\\\"><p>\\n\\n</p><h2><span data-ic=\\\"folder-v1\\\" class=\\\"pix-note-ic\\\" contenteditable=\\\"false\\\" style=\\\"color: #f66744\\\"></span>&nbsp;Pick your folder</h2><p>\\n\\n</p><ol><li>On <b>Load Images from Folder Pixaroma</b>, click <b>Browse</b> and pick your folder, or paste the folder's path into the box.</li><li>Click <b>Pick images</b>, then <b>Select all</b>, or click only the pictures you want. The button shows how many are picked.</li><li>Press <b>Run</b> once. Leave the Run count at <b>1</b>: the node sends every picture through by itself, one after the other.</li></ol><p>\\n\\n</p><p>This workflow opens with <b>no folder picked</b>: choose your own folder, or try it first on the demo folder <b>Portraits</b> inside the <b>Media Inputs</b> folder that comes with these workflows.</p><p>\\n\\n</p><p><span data-ic=\\\"idea\\\" class=\\\"pix-note-ic\\\" contenteditable=\\\"false\\\" style=\\\"color: #f66744\\\"></span>&nbsp;A folder inside ComfyUI's own <code>input</code> or <code>output</code> folder works straight away. A folder anywhere else works too, but pick it once with <b>Browse</b>: that is how ComfyUI knows you allowed it.</p><p>\\n\\n</p><p><span data-ic=\\\"idea\\\" class=\\\"pix-note-ic\\\" contenteditable=\\\"false\\\" style=\\\"color: #f66744\\\"></span>&nbsp;Pictures go through in name order. Name them <code>01_</code>, <code>02_</code> and so on if the order matters.</p><p>\\n\\n</p><hr class=\\\"pix-note-hr-solid\\\" style=\\\"color: #b8b8b8\\\"><p>\\n\\n</p><h2><span data-ic=\\\"gear\\\" class=\\\"pix-note-ic\\\" contenteditable=\\\"false\\\" style=\\\"color: #f66744\\\"></span>&nbsp;Change the look</h2><p>\\n\\n</p><ul><li>The size of each photo: <b>Resize Crop Pixaroma</b>.</li><li>The gap and its color: <b>spacing_width</b> and <b>spacing_color</b> on <b>Stitch Images</b>.</li><li>A tall strip instead of a wide one: set the direction on Stitch Images to <b>up</b>.</li></ul><p>\\n\\n</p><hr class=\\\"pix-note-hr-solid\\\" style=\\\"color: #b8b8b8\\\"><p>\\n\\n</p><h2><span data-ic=\\\"workflow-v3\\\" class=\\\"pix-note-ic\\\" contenteditable=\\\"false\\\" style=\\\"color: #f66744\\\"></span>&nbsp;How a loop works</h2><p>\\n\\n</p><ul><li>Everything between <b>Loop Start</b> and <b>Loop End</b> runs again and again: <b>total</b> on Loop Start says how many rounds.</li><li>Loop Start's <b>index</b> says which round it is, counting from <b>0</b> (0, 1, 2, 3). A Math Expression turns it into what you need: <code>a + 1</code> for 1, 2, 3, 4, or <code>a + b</code> to add it to a seed.</li><li>The <b>value</b> slots carry things from one round to the next. What you plug into Loop End's value1 comes out of Loop Start's value1 in the NEXT round. After the last round it comes out of Loop End.</li><li>Wire Loop Start's <b>loop</b> output into Loop End's <b>loop</b> input: that is how the two know they belong together.</li></ul><p>\\n\\n</p><p><span data-ic=\\\"idea\\\" class=\\\"pix-note-ic\\\" contenteditable=\\\"false\\\" style=\\\"color: #f66744\\\"></span>&nbsp;This loop needs no count from you: Get Image Size counts the photos and sets the rounds. Wiring a number into total like this works on any loop.</p><p>\\n\\n</p><hr class=\\\"pix-note-hr-solid\\\" style=\\\"color: #b8b8b8\\\"><p>\\n\\n</p><h2><span data-ic=\\\"question-mark\\\" class=\\\"pix-note-ic\\\" contenteditable=\\\"false\\\" style=\\\"color: #f66744\\\"></span>&nbsp;Something not working?</h2><p>\\n\\n</p><p>Each button opens the answer on the Pixaroma help page.</p><p>\\n\\n</p><p><span class=\\\"pix-note-btnblock\\\"><a class=\\\"pix-note-rm\\\" style=\\\"background-color: #f66744\\\" href=\\\"https://workflows.pixaroma.com/help/faq/#q-folder-not-approved\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\" rel=\\\"noopener noreferrer\\\">Folder not approved</a></span>&nbsp;<span class=\\\"pix-note-btnblock\\\"><a class=\\\"pix-note-rm\\\" style=\\\"background-color: #f66744\\\" href=\\\"https://workflows.pixaroma.com/help/faq/#q-save-other-folder\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\" rel=\\\"noopener noreferrer\\\">Save to your own folder</a></span>&nbsp;<span class=\\\"pix-note-btnblock\\\"><a class=\\\"pix-note-rm\\\" style=\\\"background-color: #f66744\\\" href=\\\"https://workflows.pixaroma.com/help/look/\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\" rel=\\\"noopener noreferrer\\\">Nodes look different from the video</a></span>&nbsp;</p><p>\\n\\n</p>\",\"buttonColor\":\"#f66744\",\"lineColor\":\"#f66744\",\"backgroundColor\":\"#2a2a2a\",\"info\":{\"title\":\"How to Use\",\"icon\":\"to-do\",\"color\":\"#2a9d8f\"}}"
