      "widgets_values": [
        "{\"version\":1,\"content\":\"<h1>WHAT EACH NODE DOES</h1><p>\\n\\n</p><p>The colour of a node tells you what kind of node it is. Nothing here needs changing except the blue ones.</p><p>\\n\\n</p><hr class=\\\"pix-note-hr-solid\\\" style=\\\"color: #b8b8b8\\\"><p>\\n\\n</p><h2><span data-ic=\\\"chip\\\" class=\\\"pix-note-ic\\\" contenteditable=\\\"false\\\" style=\\\"color: #f66744\\\"></span>&nbsp;The steps you set</h2><p>\\n\\n</p><p>Blue, and numbered. These are the only nodes you need to touch.</p><p>\\n\\n</p><ul><li><b>Load Images from Folder Pixaroma (1. your folder)</b> - Point it at a folder and pick the pictures. Press Run once and it sends every picture through the workflow, one after the other. Its <b>filename</b> output carries each picture's name to the save node, and <b>index</b> says which picture it is (1, 2, 3 ...).</li><li><b>Resize Crop Pixaroma (2. size of each photo)</b> - Makes every photo the same square size, here <b>512 x 512</b>. They must all be the same size to go into one batch.</li></ul><p>\\n\\n</p><hr class=\\\"pix-note-hr-solid\\\" style=\\\"color: #b8b8b8\\\"><p>\\n\\n</p><h2><span data-ic=\\\"chip\\\" class=\\\"pix-note-ic\\\" contenteditable=\\\"false\\\" style=\\\"color: #f66744\\\"></span>&nbsp;The helpers</h2><p>\\n\\n</p><p>Purple. They run by themselves and do the small jobs: count, pick, join or pass things along.</p><p>\\n\\n</p><ul><li><b>Rebatch Images (all photos into one batch)</b> - Collects the photos, which the folder node sends one by one, back into ONE batch, so the loop can pick them by number.</li><li><b>Get Image Size (batch_size = how many photos)</b> - Its <b>batch_size</b> output is the number of photos in the batch. It is wired into Loop Start's total, so the loop runs exactly once per photo, however many you pick.</li><li><b>Loop Start Pixaroma (one round per photo)</b> - Opens the loop. <b>total</b> comes from Get Image Size (one round per photo). <b>value1</b> carries the strip built so far: empty in round 1.</li><li><b>Loop End Pixaroma (sends the strip to the next round)</b> - Closes the loop and hands the longer strip to the next round. After the last round, value1 is the finished strip.</li></ul><p>\\n\\n</p><hr class=\\\"pix-note-hr-solid\\\" style=\\\"color: #b8b8b8\\\"><p>\\n\\n</p><h2><span data-ic=\\\"chip\\\" class=\\\"pix-note-ic\\\" contenteditable=\\\"false\\\" style=\\\"color: #f66744\\\"></span>&nbsp;The work</h2><p>\\n\\n</p><p>Green. They run by themselves.</p><p>\\n\\n</p><ul><li><b>Image From Batch (this round's photo)</b> - Takes ONE photo out of the batch: the one at this round's <b>index</b> (0 = the first photo).</li><li><b>Stitch Images (adds it to the right of the strip)</b> - Joins this round's photo and the strip so far into one picture, with a 16 px white gap. Direction <b>left</b> puts the old strip on the left, so the photos stay in order. In round 1 there is no strip yet, so the photo goes through alone.</li></ul><p>\\n\\n</p><hr class=\\\"pix-note-hr-solid\\\" style=\\\"color: #b8b8b8\\\"><p>\\n\\n</p><h2><span data-ic=\\\"checkmark\\\" class=\\\"pix-note-ic\\\" contenteditable=\\\"false\\\" style=\\\"color: #f66744\\\"></span>&nbsp;The result</h2><p>\\n\\n</p><p>Dark red, at the end.</p><p>\\n\\n</p><ul><li><b>Save Image Pixaroma (the finished strip)</b> - Saves the strip as JPG into <code>ComfyUI/output/Photo Strip</code>.</li></ul><p>\\n\\n</p><hr class=\\\"pix-note-hr-solid\\\" style=\\\"color: #b8b8b8\\\"><p>\\n\\n</p><h2><span data-ic=\\\"info\\\" class=\\\"pix-note-ic\\\" contenteditable=\\\"false\\\" style=\\\"color: #f66744\\\"></span>&nbsp;Readouts</h2><p>\\n\\n</p><p>Dark. Nothing to set: they show you what happened.</p><p>\\n\\n</p><ul><li><b>Run Timer</b> - The dark clock above the result shows how long the last Run took.</li></ul><p>\\n\\n</p>\",\"buttonColor\":\"#f66744\",\"lineColor\":\"#f66744\",\"backgroundColor\":\"#2a2a2a\",\"info\":{\"title\":\"Nodes Info\",\"icon\":\"node-v5\",\"color\":\"#3d7cc9\"}}"
      ],
      "widgets_values_named": {
        "note_json": "{\"version\":1,\"content\":\"<h1>WHAT EACH NODE DOES</h1><p>\\n\\n</p><p>The colour of a node tells you what kind of node it is. Nothing here needs changing except the blue ones.</p><p>\\n\\n</p><hr class=\\\"pix-note-hr-solid\\\" style=\\\"color: #b8b8b8\\\"><p>\\n\\n</p><h2><span data-ic=\\\"chip\\\" class=\\\"pix-note-ic\\\" contenteditable=\\\"false\\\" style=\\\"color: #f66744\\\"></span>&nbsp;The steps you set</h2><p>\\n\\n</p><p>Blue, and numbered. These are the only nodes you need to touch.</p><p>\\n\\n</p><ul><li><b>Load Images from Folder Pixaroma (1. your folder)</b> - Point it at a folder and pick the pictures. Press Run once and it sends every picture through the workflow, one after the other. Its <b>filename</b> output carries each picture's name to the save node, and <b>index</b> says which picture it is (1, 2, 3 ...).</li><li><b>Resize Crop Pixaroma (2. size of each photo)</b> - Makes every photo the same square size, here <b>512 x 512</b>. They must all be the same size to go into one batch.</li></ul><p>\\n\\n</p><hr class=\\\"pix-note-hr-solid\\\" style=\\\"color: #b8b8b8\\\"><p>\\n\\n</p><h2><span data-ic=\\\"chip\\\" class=\\\"pix-note-ic\\\" contenteditable=\\\"false\\\" style=\\\"color: #f66744\\\"></span>&nbsp;The helpers</h2><p>\\n\\n</p><p>Purple. They run by themselves and do the small jobs: count, pick, join or pass things along.</p><p>\\n\\n</p><ul><li><b>Rebatch Images (all photos into one batch)</b> - Collects the photos, which the folder node sends one by one, back into ONE batch, so the loop can pick them by number.</li><li><b>Get Image Size (batch_size = how many photos)</b> - Its <b>batch_size</b> output is the number of photos in the batch. It is wired into Loop Start's total, so the loop runs exactly once per photo, however many you pick.</li><li><b>Loop Start Pixaroma (one round per photo)</b> - Opens the loop. <b>total</b> comes from Get Image Size (one round per photo). <b>value1</b> carries the strip built so far: empty in round 1.</li><li><b>Loop End Pixaroma (sends the strip to the next round)</b> - Closes the loop and hands the longer strip to the next round. After the last round, value1 is the finished strip.</li></ul><p>\\n\\n</p><hr class=\\\"pix-note-hr-solid\\\" style=\\\"color: #b8b8b8\\\"><p>\\n\\n</p><h2><span data-ic=\\\"chip\\\" class=\\\"pix-note-ic\\\" contenteditable=\\\"false\\\" style=\\\"color: #f66744\\\"></span>&nbsp;The work</h2><p>\\n\\n</p><p>Green. They run by themselves.</p><p>\\n\\n</p><ul><li><b>Image From Batch (this round's photo)</b> - Takes ONE photo out of the batch: the one at this round's <b>index</b> (0 = the first photo).</li><li><b>Stitch Images (adds it to the right of the strip)</b> - Joins this round's photo and the strip so far into one picture, with a 16 px white gap. Direction <b>left</b> puts the old strip on the left, so the photos stay in order. In round 1 there is no strip yet, so the photo goes through alone.</li></ul><p>\\n\\n</p><hr class=\\\"pix-note-hr-solid\\\" style=\\\"color: #b8b8b8\\\"><p>\\n\\n</p><h2><span data-ic=\\\"checkmark\\\" class=\\\"pix-note-ic\\\" contenteditable=\\\"false\\\" style=\\\"color: #f66744\\\"></span>&nbsp;The result</h2><p>\\n\\n</p><p>Dark red, at the end.</p><p>\\n\\n</p><ul><li><b>Save Image Pixaroma (the finished strip)</b> - Saves the strip as JPG into <code>ComfyUI/output/Photo Strip</code>.</li></ul><p>\\n\\n</p><hr class=\\\"pix-note-hr-solid\\\" style=\\\"color: #b8b8b8\\\"><p>\\n\\n</p><h2><span data-ic=\\\"info\\\" class=\\\"pix-note-ic\\\" contenteditable=\\\"false\\\" style=\\\"color: #f66744\\\"></span>&nbsp;Readouts</h2><p>\\n\\n</p><p>Dark. Nothing to set: they show you what happened.</p><p>\\n\\n</p><ul><li><b>Run Timer</b> - The dark clock above the result shows how long the last Run took.</li></ul><p>\\n\\n</p>\",\"buttonColor\":\"#f66744\",\"lineColor\":\"#f66744\",\"backgroundColor\":\"#2a2a2a\",\"info\":{\"title\":\"Nodes Info\",\"icon\":\"node-v5\",\"color\":\"#3d7cc9\"}}"
      },
